# Copy this file to .env.local and put your Groq API key after the = sign.
# Multiple keys can be listed, separated by commas:
#   GROQ_API_KEY=key1,key2,key3
# Orbis automatically rotates to the next key when one:
#   - Is rejected (revoked or invalid)
#   - Hits a rate limit (429 error)
# .env.local is git-ignored, so keys are never pushed to GitHub.
# `npm run dev` and `npm run dist` build the keys into the app: do not share builds that contain them.
GROQ_API_KEY=

# Sign in with Google (Settings → Account). Create an OAuth client of type "Desktop app" in Google Cloud Console
# and paste its client ID and client secret here. Google gives desktop apps a "secret" that ships inside the app and
# is not treated as confidential: the sign-in is protected by PKCE, state and nonce checks instead.
# Leave these empty to hide sign-in. Use .env.development.local / .env.production.local for separate dev and release clients.
ORBIS_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
ORBIS_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
